Low-Stack HAETAE — pqm4 / mupq integration: third-party attributions
====================================================================

This bundle combines our low-stack HAETAE implementations with the pqm4 / mupq
benchmarking framework. Components remain under their respective licenses.

1. Our contribution (Apache-2.0)
--------------------------------
The HAETAE low-stack implementation files under
    crypto_sign/haetae{2,3,5}/C/
    crypto_sign/haetae{2,3,5}/asm/
that we authored or modified for this work carry an Apache 2.0 license header at
the top of the file (see any such file, e.g. sign_passes.c, encoding.c, keygen.c,
verify.c). Files that are verbatim from the upstream HAETAE reference, or are
third-party headers, do not carry our header and are covered by their own
license (see below). Presence of the Apache 2.0 header is authoritative.

2. pqm4 / mupq framework (Apache-2.0 or CC0-1.0)
------------------------------------------------
The build system, test/benchmark harnesses and platform support — Makefile,
mk/, mupq/ (mupq.py, platforms.py, mk/, common/, crypto_sign/ harness sources),
common/, ldscripts/, benchmarks.py, test.py, interface.py, st_nucleo_l4r5.cfg —
are from the pqm4 project and remain under "Apache-2.0 or CC0-1.0" (the SPDX tag
carried in those files). Upstream: https://github.com/mupq/pqm4 (and its mupq
submodule https://github.com/mupq/mupq).

3. SHA-3 / SHAKE / Keccak, AES, NIST seed expander
--------------------------------------------------
common/keccakf1600.{c,S}, mupq/common/fips202.{c,h},
mupq/pqclean/common/{fips202,aes,sha2,sp800-185,nistseedexpander,...} and the
shared headers symlinked from mupq/common/ are from pqm4/PQClean and are public
domain / CC0 (or as stated in each file).

4. rANS coder
-------------
crypto_sign/haetae*/{C,asm}/rans_byte.h is the public-domain rANS implementation
by Fabian Giesen.

5. CMSIS / MPS2 platform support
--------------------------------
common/mps2/* (startup, linker script, system support for the QEMU MPS2 target)
is ARM CMSIS / MPS2 material under Apache-2.0.

6. HAETAE reference
-------------------
The HAETAE scheme and its reference implementation are by the HAETAE team
(CryptoLab); the Cortex-M4 reference port is from pqm4. Unmodified reference
files are left under their original licensing.
